	regionKind = "dungeon",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Temple of Atal'Hakkar lies drowned beneath the {link:pool-of-tears}Pool of Tears{/link} in the {link:swamp-of-sorrows}Swamp of Sorrows{/link}. It was raised by the Atal'ai, a sect of troll priests, as a shrine to {link:hakkar}Hakkar{/link} the Soulflayer, the blood god of the {link:trolls}trolls{/link}. Its upper stones still break the surface of the water. The rest has sunk into the mire. Green dragons keep watch over the ruin, and they let no one in or out. Yet the Atal'ai have not left it. Deep below the swamp they still keep their rites, and they still wait for their god.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The Atal'ai were once priests of the Gurubashi, the great troll empire of the south. After the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link} cost the empire much of its land, they called {link:hakkar}Hakkar{/link} into the world at {link:zul-gurub}Zul'Gurub{/link}. The god demanded blood, and he fed on the very people who worshipped him. At last the Gurubashi tribes rose against him. They cast him out and drove his priests from the jungle.

The exiles fled north into the swamps. There they built a great temple to their god, where they meant to prepare for his return to the physical world. The Aspect of the green dragonflight, {red:ysera}Ysera{/red}, learned of their plans. She broke the temple and sank it beneath the marsh. Her dragons have guarded the drowned ruins ever since, so that the Atal'ai may never again bring Hakkar forth.

No chronicle of these days agrees on the year the temple was built, or the year it sank.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The sinking did not end the Atal'ai. Some survived beneath the water, and they gave themselves once more to the service of their god. Their spiritual leader is {link:jammal-an-the-prophet}Jammal'an the Prophet{/link}. He has had a vision, and he preaches that when {link:hakkar}Hakkar{/link} returns to {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}, the god will grant the Atal'ai immortality. Priests who doubted him have been cast out. One of them, the {link:atal-ai-exile}Atal'ai Exile{/link}, now lives among the {link:witherbark-trolls}Witherbark trolls{/link} of {link:the-hinterlands}The Hinterlands{/link}.

The guardians of the temple have fared no better than its builders. The dragon Eranikus was charged with keeping the trolls from ever raising their god again. Now his mind is failing, and only his shade stirs in the temple's depths. The green dragonkin who serve him are called by the name of nightmare, and they strike at every intruder, whatever the intruder's purpose.

The world has taken notice. The Warchief of the {link:horde}Horde{/link} sent {link:fel-zerul}Fel'zerul{/link} to {link:stonard}Stonard{/link} to learn what happened here, and he wants the fetishes that the Atal'ai use in their summoning. {link:brohann-caskbelly}Brohann Caskbelly{/link} of the {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} wants the temple's tablets for his last great discovery. In {link:tanaris}Tanaris{/link}, the troll {link:yeh-kinya}Yeh'kinya{/link} has learned of a way to capture the essence of Hakkar and keep it from those who would use it. Others seek the drakes of the depths for reasons of their own.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Within the Temple",
			text = [=[• {b}The Drowned Halls.{/b} Broken stairs and flooded passages, where murk worms, oozes and lurkers from the deep have made their home among the ruins.
• {b}The Circle of Statues.{/b} A round hall with six balconies, a serpent statue on the edge of each, and an altar of {link:hakkar}Hakkar{/link} at its base. It hides the Atal'ai's treasure and its guardian, {link:atal-alarion}Atal'alarion{/link}.
• {b}The Chamber of Blood.{/b} The seat of {link:jammal-an-the-prophet}Jammal'an{/link} and his disciples, sealed behind a barrier that six troll guardians hold.
• {b}The Sanctum of the Fallen God.{/b} Here eternal flames hold the spirit of Hakkar, tended by the bloodkeepers of the god.
• {b}The Lair of Eranikus.{/b} The upper halls, held by his drakes and dragonkin. Here stands the essence font of the green dragonflight.]=],
		},
	},
})

