	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Hakkar the Soulflayer is the blood god of the {link:trolls}trolls{/link}, a loa of terrible hunger. The trolls worship many spirits, but none is feared as he is. Where Hakkar is honored, blood is spilled. His servants among the living are the Atal'ai, a sect of priests who once served the Gurubashi Empire. His winged serpents still haunt the places where he was worshipped, and the trolls say the wind serpents of the wild are his kin.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[Hakkar nearly destroyed the troll empire of the south. After the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}, the Gurubashi had lost much of their land, and their priests turned to dark power in their need. The Atal'ai called Hakkar into the world at {link:zul-gurub}Zul'Gurub{/link}. He came, and he demanded blood. He fed on the very people who had summoned him. At last the tribes of the Gurubashi rose against the god and his priests. They cast him down and drove the Atal'ai into exile. The empire never recovered. Its tribes turned on one another, and its cities were left to the jungle.

The Atal'ai did not lose their faith. In the {link:swamp-of-sorrows}Swamp of Sorrows{/link} they raised a temple to him, and there they made ready for his return. {red:ysera}Ysera{/red} sank that temple beneath the swamp, and her dragons have watched it ever since. It was not enough. The Atal'ai who survived still work in its depths to call him back from the Nether.

The trolls tell two tales of him. In one, his coming will bring joy and glory to all trollkind. In the other, his return will mark the end of all things. Those who have seen what his priests have done believe the second.

The Atal'ai are not his only servants. In the {link:the-hinterlands}Hinterlands{/link}, the {red:vilebranch-trolls}Vilebranch{/red} offer captives to him in their capital of {link:jintha-alor}Jintha'Alor{/link}, where vessels of tainted blood drive them to madness.]=],
